# Everything the pipeline downloads, records or generates lives under data/, and
# everything a run produces lands in output/, so the repo root stays clean.
# Neither is tracked:
#
#   data/external/      audioset, fma, mit_rirs, oww feature .npy, cloned repos
#   data/piper_voices/  piper voices, pulled on demand into the container volume
#   data/recordings/    real samples, raw takes, holdout   (1 · record)
#   data/corpus/        generated positives / negatives    (2 · train)
#   data/corpus/eval/   the TTS evaluation corpora         (3 · eval)
#   data/audit/         tools/ one-off measurement output
#
#   output/             trained oww + mww models, training_config.yaml, scorecards
data/
output/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
.venv-*/

# The openWakeWord clone that scripts/setup-applesilicon-trainer.sh makes at the repo
# root. It is upstream's code plus our patches applied in place - reproducible from
# that script, and never ours to commit. train/oww/train.py resolves it as
# WORK_DIR/"openwakeword/...", which is why it sits here rather than out of the way.
# .dockerignore excludes it too: inside a build context it would shadow the clone each
# image makes for itself, with one patched for a different device.
openwakeword/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# OS / IDE / archives
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.zip
.claude/settings.json

# training logs
*.log
